-- lib/os/contract.cub — the contract of the kernel, as a world (archive/2026-11-11/PLAN-rev9.md, revision 9, 9 Nov 2026, sha256 4d012c3a10fd…, §6 “Phases 2–8: everything that will be built”, “Phase 3 — The OS as a world”, item 1 “The syscall world”, and §7 “The trusted base, exactly (revision 9)”:
-- trusted until the kernel is lifted). Loaded after lib/os/linux.cub.
--
-- linux-model : World Linux KState answers each command of Linux from a state: this is the
-- statement of what a process may assume of the kernel, and what a property of a process over
-- Linux is proved against (runp p linux-model st computes; lib/proc.cub). It is deterministic
-- and it is a subset: what the kernel may do that the model does not say (a descriptor kind
-- outside it, a wait nothing in the state will end) the model refuses, so a run that reaches it
-- ends `stopped` and nothing is claimed about it.
--
-- The state: memory as bytes at addresses with the regions that are mapped (an access outside
-- them is EFAULT in a system call and the end of the process in a peek or poke); the descriptor
-- table (the lowest free number is the next); pipe ends (a read end holds the bytes still to be
-- read and has no writer left, so empty is end of file; a write end holds what was written); UDP
-- sockets (bound or not); epoll instances (their interest lists); the datagrams that will arrive,
-- in order (k-net: a receive takes the first addressed to the socket), and those sent to
-- addresses no socket here is bound to, in order (k-sent: what left the host); a clock in
-- nanoseconds (a reading advances it by k-tick, a sleep by its length); the port the next
-- unbound sender is given; the page size; the pid; the exit status once the process has ended.
--
-- Answered: clock_gettime, nanosleep, read and write (pipes; read on a socket), close, socket
-- (AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM), bind, recvfrom (flags 0, or MSG_DONTWAIT), sendto, setsockopt, listen
-- and accept4 (EOPNOTSUPP on a datagram socket), mmap (anonymous, private, address chosen by the
-- kernel), munmap (a whole mapping), mprotect (to read|write, which every region is),
-- epoll_create1, epoll_ctl, epoll_wait (level-triggered readiness), futex wake (no waiter: 0)
-- and wait (EAGAIN on a different value), getpid, exit_group (the status recorded, the process
-- ended), and the memory commands. Refused: open, connect, a blocking receive with nothing to
-- arrive, an epoll_wait without timeout with nothing ready, a futex wait that would sleep.
record Dgram = { dg-from : SockAddr ; dg-to : SockAddr ; dg-data : List Word }
